Problem: Trapping Rain Water (LC 42)

Pattern: Two Pointers

Approach:

1. Initialize left = 0 and right = height.size() - 1.
2. Initialize leftMax = 0, rightMax = 0, and water = 0.
3. Compare height[left] and height[right].
4. If height[left] < height[right], process the left side.
5. If height[left] >= leftMax, update leftMax.
6. Otherwise, add leftMax - height[left] to water.
7. Move left++.
8. Otherwise, process the right side.
9. If height[right] >= rightMax, update rightMax.
10. Otherwise, add rightMax - height[right] to water.
11. Move right--.
12. Continue until left < right is false.
13. Return water.

Key idea:
leftMax = tallest wall seen from the left.
rightMax = tallest wall seen from the right.
Water = maximum wall - current bar height.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
